 -  assumes you hava java-21
 -  running 'mvn clean install' will build the image
 -  you can check that via 'docker images | grep sample'

 -  create local cluster: 'kind create cluster'
 -  load the image into the cluster : 'kind load docker-image sample:latest'

 - deploy all manifests from k8s directory:
    'kubectl apply -f .'

 - run 'docker ps' to find the container ID

 - run 'docker exec -u 0 --privileged -it <CONTAINER_ID> bash'

 - find the IP of the pod:
   'kubectl get pods -o wide'

 - issue 'curl 10.244.0.5:8080/value' (nothing is returned)

 - issue 'curl 10.244.0.5:8080/valueDev' ('my.dev.property' is returned)

 proves that the correct file is read.















